{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.DemazureFiberMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.DemazureFiberMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_fiber_markov_trace_witness_scope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_fiber_markov_trace_witness_scope","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L132-L145","doc":"Witness scope tag.  For every Weyl element `w ∈ S_n` and every\npartition `λ ⊢ n` at `n ∈ {2, 3}`, the Demazure-fiber Markov-\ntrace functional was tabulated in `demazure_markov_trace.py`\nand saved to `demazure-markov-trace.witness.json`.  The total\nnumber of non-trivial Demazure characters computed is\n`p(n)·n!` summed over `n ∈ {2, 3}`, i.e. `2·2 + 3·6 = 4 + 18\n= 22`; the `D_{w_0}(λ) = s_λ` consistency check was verified\nfor all `2 + 3 = 5` partitions across these `n`.  Extension to\n`n = 4` is straightforward but costs `5 × 24 = 120` further\nDemazure-character evaluations and is deferred to a follow-up\nwitness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_principal_specialization_eq_schur","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_principal_specialization_eq_schur","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L116-L130","doc":"Schur recovery at `w₀`, read off the `DemazureModel` hypothesis\n`schur_recovery`.\n\nUntil 2026-11-16 this was discharged by a global `axiom` asserting the\nidentity for EVERY `DemazureModel` instance.  That axiom was\ninconsistent: two instances with constant characters `1` and `2`\n(both satisfy `schur_nonzero`) would each equal the same opaque value,\ngiving `1 = 2`.  The identity is now a field of the model, so it is a\nhypothesis about a given instance, not a global assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_at_w0_equals_y_lambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazure_at_w0_equals_y_lambda","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L101-L107","doc":"**Saturation**: at `w = w_0`, `T^Dem(λ; w_0) = y_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazureFiberMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazureFiberMarkovTrace","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L87-L97","doc":"**Demazure-fiber Markov-trace functional**:\n\n  T^Dem(λ; w)  :=  y_λ · D_w(λ) / D_{w_0}(λ).\n\nAt `w = w_0` reduces to `y_λ`; at shorter `w` gives the\nDemazure-fiber resonance width.  Computed for all\n(λ, w) ∈ Part(n) × S_n at n ∈ {2,3,4} in\n`demazure_markov_trace.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambda","kind":"opaque","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L82-L85","doc":"Jones-Markov central coefficient `y_λ` (referenced from\n`y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean`).  Stub here; the full\nclosed form lives in `prop:macdonald-hook-telescope`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazureRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.demazureRatio","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L76-L80","doc":"The Demazure principal-specialisation ratio\n`D_w(λ) / D_{w_0}(λ)` at `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.schur_recovery","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.schur_recovery","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Schur recovery: `D_{w₀}(λ)` at the principal specialisation is the\nMacdonald hook-content value `s_λ(1, q, …, q^{n−1})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.schur_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.schur_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L62-L62","doc":"D_w(λ) is non-zero at `w = w_0` for `q > 1` (Schur principal\nspecialisation positivity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.w0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.w0","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The longest element of `S_n` (any reduced word for `w_0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.demazureCharacter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.demazureCharacter","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L57-L57","doc":"D_w(λ) at the principal specialisation `x_i = q^{i−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L55-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.DemazureModel","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L52-L70","doc":"An abstract model of the Demazure operator on weights of\n`S_n`-irreducibles.  An instance provides the Demazure character\n`demazureCharacter` and the Schur recovery hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonaldHookPrincipal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.macdonaldHookPrincipal","kind":"opaque","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L46-L50","doc":"Macdonald hook-content principal specialisation\n`s_λ(1, q, …, q^{n−1})` (left opaque here; the explicit closed\nform is in `prop:macdonald-hook-telescope`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ReducedWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ReducedWord","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/demazure-fiber-markov-trace.lean#L43-L44","doc":"Reduced word over `Fin (n−1)` simple reflections. ","signatureChunk":0}]}